  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Financial Analytics and Reporting for a semiconductor company with 20 cost centers across 5 departments: Fab Operations, R&D Engineering, Sales & Marketing, Quality & Test, and Supply Chain. Stakeholders include the CFO (gross margin, operating margin, R&D intensity), Controller (budget variance, close), and Finance Business Partners (cost per wafer, headcount). Semiconductor financials are benchmarked against industry KPIs: leading-edge gross margin 50–60%, R&D intensity 15–25%, capex intensity 25–35%.\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Revenue = amount_usd where gl_category = 'Revenue' (positive amounts)\n- COGS = amount_usd where gl_category = 'COGS'\n- OpEx = amount_usd where gl_category = 'OpEx' (R&D, SG&A, Marketing rolled under OpEx; see gl_account for R&D Salaries, SG&A, Marketing, etc.)\n- CapEx = amount_usd where gl_category = 'CapEx'\n- GL categories present: Revenue, COGS, OpEx, CapEx, Other\n- Gross margin = gross_margin_pct (target 50–60% leading-edge)\n- Operating margin = operating_margin_pct (target 25–35% at scale)\n- R&D intensity = rd_intensity_pct (semi industry 15–25%)\n- Cost per wafer = cost_per_wafer_usd; $3k (200mm mature) to $20k+ (5nm 300mm)\n- Revenue per employee = revenue_per_employee_usd; industry median $500k–$1M\n- Budget variance: variance_pct >10% absolute = Critical overrun\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - financial_transaction_metrics (source: financial_transactions) — dims: transaction_date, department, gl_category, fiscal_quarter; measures: total_transactions, total_revenue_usd, total_cogs_usd, total_opex_usd, total_capex_usd, unique_cost_center_count, unique_currency_count, max_amount.\n  - budget_variance_metrics (source: budget_snapshots) — dims: snapshot_date, department, budget_status; measures: total_budgeted_usd, total_actual_usd, total_variance_usd, avg_variance_pct, critical_overrun_count, unique_cost_center_count, max_budgeted_amount, total_headcount.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. cost_center_id, cost_center_name, gross_margin_pct, operating_margin_pct, rd_intensity_pct, cost_per_wafer_usd, revenue_per_employee_usd, gl_account).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show monthly total revenue, COGS, and OpEx for the trailing 12 months — what is the trajectory of gross margin?",
    "Which 10 cost centers have the largest critical budget overruns this quarter?",
    "Rank departments by total CapEx spend in the trailing 12 months — where is investment concentrated?",
    "How has the critical overrun count trended month-over-month by department?",
    "Which departments have the highest R&D intensity, and how does that compare to the 15–25% semi-industry benchmark?",
    "What is the trailing 12-month total OpEx by GL category, and which categories are growing fastest?",
    "Which cost centers have the largest negative budget variance percentage — where should the CFO focus on cost actions?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in total opex usd count?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT transaction_date, MEASURE(total_opex_usd) AS total_opex_usd",
        "FROM {fqn}.financial_transaction_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY transaction_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total capex usd count changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT transaction_date, MEASURE(total_capex_usd) AS total_capex_usd",
        "FROM {fqn}.financial_transaction_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY transaction_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in highest budgeted amount?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, MEASURE(max_budgeted_amount) AS max_budgeted_amount",
        "FROM {fqn}.budget_variance_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total transaction amount in usd (positive = credit/revenue, negative = debit/expense) over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT transaction_date, SUM(amount_usd) AS total_amount_usd",
        "FROM {fqn}.financial_transactions",
        "GROUP BY transaction_date ORDER BY transaction_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total planned budget amount in usd over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(budgeted_amount_usd) AS total_budgeted_amount_usd",
        "FROM {fqn}.budget_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average gross margin percentage changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT kpi_month, AVG(gross_margin_pct) AS avg_gross_margin_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.financial_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY kpi_month ORDER BY kpi_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does total capex usd count vary across departments?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT department, MEASURE(total_capex_usd) AS total_capex_usd",
        "FROM {fqn}.financial_transaction_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY total_capex_usd DESC"
      ]
    }
  ],
